#. はぁーあ……
msgctxt "0001 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "*Sigh*"
msgstr ""

#. …どうしたの？
#. なんか、重いため息だね…
msgctxt "0002 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "What's wrong? That seemed like a pretty heavy sigh..."
msgstr ""

#. なんか…申し訳なくて…
msgctxt "0003 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "Oh, sorry..."
msgstr ""

#. みんなが頑張って、出る方法を探してるのに…
#. 全然役に立ててないから…
msgctxt "0004 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"It's just, everyone else is working so hard to get us\n"
"out of here, but I'm no help at all."
msgstr ""

#. そ、そんな事ないよ！
msgctxt "0005 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "Th-That's not true at all!"
msgstr ""

#. …いいんだ。本当の事だから。
msgctxt "0006 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"It's okay, you don't have to try and make me feel\n"
"better. I know it's the truth."
msgstr ""

#. どうせ、パソコンがなければ何も出来ないし…
msgctxt "0007 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"I'm completely useless without a computer in front of\n"
"me..."
msgstr ""

#. せめて、もう少し体力があれば、
#. ちょっとは、みんなの役に立てたのに…
msgctxt "0008 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"At least if I were a little stronger or something,\n"
"then I'd be able to help somehow..."
msgstr ""

#. …でも、きっといつか来るはずだよ。
#. 不二咲さんの能力が必要な時がさ…
msgctxt "0009 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"Listen, you'll get your chance. I'm sure there'll be a\n"
"time when your skills will come in handy."
msgstr ""

#. だからさ、そんなに焦らなくても大丈夫だよ。
msgctxt "0010 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "So you don't have to worry so much, okay?"
msgstr ""

#. 能力が…必要な時…
msgctxt "0011 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "My skills might...come in handy?"
msgstr ""

#. そうしたら…役に立てるように頑張るね…
#. <CLT 3>コンピューター<CLT>の事なら自信あるから…
msgctxt "0012 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"If I get a chance, I'm gonna work super hard to chip\n"
"in! When it comes to <CLT 3>computers<CLT>, you can count on me!"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>そうだよな…なんと言っても、
#. <CLT><CLT 3>“超高校級のプログラマー”<CLT><CLT 4>なんだもんな…
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0013 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>You're right about that. No matter what anyone might\n"
"say, you're still the <CLT><CLT 3>Ultimate Programmer<CLT><CLT 4>!\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. …でもさ、不二咲さんはどうして、
#. プログラミングを始めたの？
msgctxt "0014 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "Speaking of which, how did you get into programming?"
msgstr ""

#. …え？
msgctxt "0015 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "Huh...?"
msgstr ""

#. いや、プログラムとかって、
#. やっぱり男性がやるイメージがあるからさ…
msgctxt "0016 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"Well, I mean...I always assumed most programmers were\n"
"guys, so..."
msgstr ""

#. ………………
msgctxt "0017 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "..."
msgstr "..."

#. 変…かな…？
msgctxt "0018 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "Is it really that weird...?"
msgstr ""

#. い、いや…そうじゃなくって、
#. 理由が気になっただけなんだよ。
msgctxt "0019 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"N-No, nothing like that! I was just curious what got\n"
"you interested in it."
msgstr ""

#. 不二咲さんが、
#. プログラミングをするようになった理由がさ…
msgctxt "0020 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "I mean, why programming of all things?"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 3>理由<CLT>…
msgctxt "0021 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "<CLT 3>Why<CLT>...?"
msgstr ""

#. 理由はね、大した事じゃないんだ…
msgctxt "0022 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "I mean, there isn't much of a reason."
msgstr ""

#. 子供の頃から体が弱くてさ、
#. 外で友達と駆け回ったり出来なくて…
msgctxt "0023 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"I've always been kind of weak, ya know. I was never\n"
"able to run around with my friends or anything..."
msgstr ""

#. だから、ヒマ潰しに家にあるパソコンをいじったら、
#. それが思った以上に楽しくってさぁ…
msgctxt "0024 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"We had a computer at home, so I'd kill time poking\n"
"around with it. And I found out I really liked it!"
msgstr ""

#. でね、お父さんがシステムエンジニアでさ、
#. 仕事で色んなプログラムを組んでたんだけど…
msgctxt "0025 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"My dad was a software engineer, and he had a bunch of\n"
"programs on there that he'd built."
msgstr ""

#. …お父さんの作成途中のプログラムを見つけて、
#. 勝手にそれを改造して遊んでたんだ…
msgctxt "0026 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"I found one of them and started playing around with\n"
"it, adding stuff here and there..."
msgstr ""

#. そうやって出来たのが…
#. 最初に、自分で組んだプログラムだよ。
msgctxt "0027 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"And that was how I ended up making my very first\n"
"program."
msgstr ""

#. どういうプログラムだったの？
msgctxt "0028 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "Interesting... What kind of program was it?"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 3>自動応答システム<CLT>だよ。
msgctxt "0029 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "A kind of <CLT 3>database software<CLT>..."
msgstr ""

#. …自動応答システム？
msgctxt "0030 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "Database software..."
msgstr ""

#. ユーザーとの対話を通して、言葉を理解し、
#. ユーザーが求める情報を見つけ出すシステムだよ。
msgctxt "0031 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"A user could communicate with it, and it would take\n"
"that information and find what they were looking for."
msgstr ""

#. つまり、キーボード入力以外の方法で
#. コンピューターとやり取り出来るシステムだね。
msgctxt "0032 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"It was a way of interacting with the computer without\n"
"having to physically type things out."
msgstr ""

#. 音声入力
msgctxt "0033 | CHOICE/RE:ACT"
msgid "Voice recognition"
msgstr ""

#. タッチ入力
msgctxt "0034 | CHOICE/RE:ACT"
msgid "Touchscreen"
msgstr ""

#. タッチ入力かな？
#. 画面にさわって直接、入力するやつ。
msgctxt "0035 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "Was it through, like, touchscreen or something?"
msgstr ""

#. そういう方法もあるけど…
#. その時に使ったのは別なんだ。
msgctxt "0036 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"Well, that did exist back then, but I did something\n"
"different."
msgstr ""

#. 指や手も使わないで、
#. 画面にさわる事もしないで入力する方法だよ。
msgctxt "0037 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"I wanted to find a way to interact with a computer\n"
"without having to use your hands."
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>指も手も？
#. となると…
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0038 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>Without using your hands? Then...\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. 念力で入力
msgctxt "0039 | CHOICE/RE:ACT"
msgid "Telekinesis"
msgstr ""

#. 念力で入力とか？
#. 動けって念じると、コンピューターが反応するとか。
msgctxt "0040 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"Did you use telekinesis? As soon as you think\n"
"something, the computer reacts, that kind of ting?"
msgstr ""

#. うふふ、ＳＦ小説みたい…
#. 面白い事言うんだねぇ、苗木君。
msgctxt "0041 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"Hehe. That sounds like something out of a sci-fi\n"
"movie. You're so funny, Makoto!"
msgstr ""

#. でも、そういう入力方法が確立されるのは
#. ずっと、ずーっと先の未来かなぁ…
msgctxt "0042 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"But I think it'll be a while before we figure out how\n"
"to do something like that..."
msgstr ""

#. その時に使ったのはね…
msgctxt "0043 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "No, I used something different."
msgstr ""

#. 念力じゃなくて、あることで
#. コンピューターに意志を伝える方法だよ。
msgctxt "0044 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"It wasn't with psychic power, but it *was* a way to\n"
"convey information without touching the computer."
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>コンピューターに意志を伝える？
#. つまり…
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0045 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>Convey information to the computer...? In other\n"
"words...\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. ちょっと難しいかなぁ？
msgctxt "0046 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "Are you having trouble understanding the idea?"
msgstr ""

#. もっと簡単に言うとね、
#. コンピューターとお話しをするって感じかな。
msgctxt "0047 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"It was simply a way of communicating with the computer\n"
"more directly."
msgstr ""

#. コンピューターとお話しを？
#. ええっと、それは…
msgctxt "0048 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "Communicating more directly? So you mean..."
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>ユーザーとの対話を通して言葉を理解する、
#. キーボード以外の入力方法…
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0049 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>She said it could understand the user without them\n"
"having to type things out...\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>それって、つまり…
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0050 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>So that would have to be...\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. …音声入力？
msgctxt "0051 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "You used voice recognition, is that it?"
msgstr ""

#. うん、そうなんだ！
msgctxt "0052 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "Yup, exactly!"
msgstr ""

#. 応答の声に自分の声を使ったら、
#. それと会話してるのが面白くなっちゃってさ…
msgctxt "0053 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"You could talk to it, and it could actually talk back.\n"
"It was a lot of fun!"
msgstr ""

#. なんか、自分の声じゃないみたいなんだもん！
#. 夢中で色々やってたら、出来ちゃった。
msgctxt "0054 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"It didn't even really sound like me! I would get\n"
"totally absorbed in talking to it..."
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>子供が自分の声を録音して聞いて遊ぶのと同じ…
#. いや違うな、遊びにしては高度過ぎるし…
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0055 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>It's like a kid recording themselves and playing it\n"
"back again...\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. このシステムの肝となるのは、
#. 情報が正しく入力されるかって点なんだけどさ…
msgctxt "0056 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"The key part of the program was getting it to\n"
"recognize what I was saying."
msgstr ""

#. つまり、音声入力の精度だね。
#. 日本語って複雑だから苦労したんだぁ。
msgctxt "0057 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"The recognition accuracy was the most important thing.\n"
"Japanese is kinda hard, so it was pretty challenging."
msgstr ""

#. でも、それを完成させたの？
msgctxt "0058 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "But you were able to do it eventually?"
msgstr ""

#. しかも、ちょうど完成させた頃…
msgctxt "0059 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "Yup! And right around then..."
msgstr ""

#. 勝手にプログラムを改造してたのが
#. お父さんに見つかっちゃってさぁ…
msgctxt "0060 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"...my dad found out I'd messed with his software\n"
"without permission."
msgstr ""

#. 怒られると思ったんだけど…
msgctxt "0061 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "I thought I was gonna get in so much trouble..."
msgstr ""

#. 逆にね、すっごく<CLT 3>褒められた<CLT>んだよ！
msgctxt "0062 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "But all he said was how <CLT 3>impressed<CLT> he was!"
msgstr ""

#. あのシステムは、自然言語理解にも取り組んでて、
#. それによる対話型の情報絞り込みをやってたんだけど…
msgctxt "0063 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"The software was able to take natural speech and pull\n"
"out key search terms to retrieve information."
msgstr ""

#. その操作性がすごく良かったみたいで、
#. 情報検索の歴史が変わるぞとまで褒められたんだ！
msgctxt "0064 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"My dad said it worked so well, it was gonna change the\n"
"face of software interaction all over the world!"
msgstr ""

#. 実際は、コストの問題で、
#. まだまだ普及には至ってないんだけど…
msgctxt "0065 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"The development costs are still pretty expensive, so\n"
"it hasn't spread that much yet, but..."
msgstr ""

#. でも、それ以来、
#. プログラミングに夢中になっちゃってさ…
msgctxt "0066 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"Anyway, I've been addicted to programming ever\n"
"since..."
msgstr ""

#. こんな自分でも人を喜ばせられたって事が、
#. 嬉しくって！
msgctxt "0067 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"I can't tell you how happy it made me to be able to\n"
"make others happy...!"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>不二咲さん…
#. 本当にコンピューターが好きなんだな…
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0068 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>It's obvious how much you love computers.\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>だって、その話になると、
#. すごく生き生きしてるもんな。
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0069 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>You seem to just...light up when you start talking\n"
"about them.\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. …あ！　ごめんね！
#. なんか勝手に１人で喋っちゃった！
msgctxt "0070 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid ""
"Ah! Sorry, I spent all this time just talking about\n"
"myself..."
msgstr ""

#. ううん、すごく面白かったよ。
#. 不二咲さんの話…
msgctxt "0071 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "No, I had a lot of fun learning more about you!"
msgstr ""

#. え？　ホントに…？
msgctxt "0072 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "Huh? Really...?"
msgstr ""

#. だからさ、また不二咲さんの話を聞かせてよ。
msgctxt "0073 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid "Yup! I hope you'll tell me even more next time."
msgstr ""

#. う、うん…！
#. じゃあ、また一緒にお話しようね！
msgctxt "0074 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "O-Okay! Let's hang out again sometime!"
msgstr ""

#. えへへ！　約束だよぉ！？
msgctxt "0075 | CHIHIRO FUJISAKI"
msgid "It's a promise, okay?"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 23>不二咲千尋の<CLT><CLT 3>通信簿<CLT><CLT 23>に、今の情報を追記致しました。
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0076 | NARRATION"
msgid ""
"<CLT 23>Chihiro's <CLT><CLT 3>Report Card<CLT><CLT 23> has been updated based on your\n"
"experience with her.\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 23>おめでとうございます。
#. スキル<CLT><CLT 3>“アルゴリズム”<CLT><CLT 23>を獲得致しました。
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0077 | NARRATION"
msgid ""
"<CLT 23>You just unlocked the skill <CLT><CLT 3>Algorithm<CLT><CLT 23>!\n"
"Give yourself a pat on the back. You've earned it!\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""

#. <CLT 4>不二咲さんと別れた後、
#. ボクは自分の部屋に帰った。
#. <CLT>
msgctxt "0078 | MAKOTO NAEGI"
msgid ""
"<CLT 4>I parted ways with Chihiro, and went back to my room.\n"
"<CLT>"
msgstr ""
